# Mermaid spacing and color in docs

When writing or editing `docs/**/*.mdx`, add **`<br/>`** on its own line immediately after every ` ```mermaid ` closing fence, and **color every node** with `classDef` (do not ship grey default mermaid).

Reference: `docs/frameworks/gain-mcp.mdx`, `docs/insights/2026-08-05-one-agent-routes-vs-specialized-agents/one-agent-routes-vs-specialized-agents.mdx`.

## Required pattern (bare mermaid)

1. Open with a ` ```mermaid ` fenced block and close it with ` ``` `.
2. On the **next line**, add `<br/>`.
3. Then the heading, paragraph, or table.

Example shape (closing fence, then spacer, then prose):

    [mermaid fence open]
    flowchart LR
        A --> B
    [mermaid fence close]
    <br/>
    ## Next section

## Wrapped in `gain-mermaid` (framework pages)

When the fence is inside `<div className="gain-mermaid">`, put `<br/>` after `</div>`:

    <br/>
    <div className="gain-mermaid">
    [mermaid fence + diagram]
    </div>
    <br/>

Optional `<br/>` before the wrapper is fine for top spacing. **After** the diagram is required.

## Color nodes (`classDef`)

Unstyled mermaid is grey. Assign a role to every node. Reuse this palette; do not invent a new hex set per page.

| Role | Typical nodes | `classDef` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Actor / input | User, client, request | `fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#93c5fd,color:#1e293b,stroke-width:2px` |
| Gate | Router, policy, PEP, safety | `fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#fdba74,color:#1e293b,stroke-width:2px` |
| Process | Routes, agents, LLM, runtime steps | `fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#c4b5fd,color:#1e293b,stroke-width:2px` |
| Shared / platform | Shared runtime, policy platform, state | `fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#86efac,color:#1e293b,stroke-width:2px` |
| Action / source | Tool execution, catalogs, sources | `fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#fcd34d,color:#1e293b,stroke-width:2px` |

    [mermaid fence open]
    flowchart TB
        User["① User"] --> Router["② Intent Router"]
        Router --> Runtime["③ Shared runtime"]

        classDef actor fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#93c5fd,color:#1e293b,stroke-width:2px
        classDef gate fill:#ffedd5,stroke:#fdba74,color:#1e293b,stroke-width:2px
        classDef runtime fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#86efac,color:#1e293b,stroke-width:2px

        class User actor
        class Router gate
        class Runtime runtime
    [mermaid fence close]
    <br/>

Map with `class NodeName role`. Insights use a bare mermaid fence. Framework pages may wrap in `<div className="gain-mermaid">`.

## Do not add

- `<br/>` inside the mermaid fence (breaks the diagram).
- Duplicate `<br/>` between consecutive diagrams unless prose sits between them.

## Before finishing

1. Every ` ```mermaid ` block in changed `.mdx` files has `<br/>` after the closing fence (or after `</div>` when wrapped).
2. Every node in those diagrams has a `classDef` color (no grey defaults).
3. When editing a section with mermaid, fix spacing and color on blocks you touch; do not bulk-rewrite unrelated diagrams.
